wyMzA0OTQ4MTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:codestyle","name":"topic:codestyle","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-07-19T10:24:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T08:10:35Z","closed_at":"2026-07-22T01:26:40Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121547","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121547","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121547.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121547.patch","merged_at":"2026-07-22T01:26:39Z"},"body":"Splits AudioServer files and system classes.\r\n\r\n\r\n- Moved enums, structs and types to dedicated files so not everything includes the entire audio server and system.\r\nThe old enums can now all be found under `servers/audio/audio_server_enums.h`\r\nThe old constants can now all be found under `servers/audio/audio_server_constants.h`\r\nThe old structs can now all be found under `servers/audio/audio_server_types.h`\r\n\r\n(jk that last structs  file is empty but I left it in so the audio guys know where to place and not have so many merge conflicts moving stuff next).\r\n\r\n- Splits `AudioDriver` and `AudioBusLayout` from `AudioServer`.\r\nMany classes need the driver included but have zero use for the entire server.\r\nNote that some thirdparty or platform audio classes have internal mumbo making it difficult to forward declare in the current state so I left them mostly.\r\nThe platform support guys can solve their own stuff. E.g. I dont have a Mac, or interest to do Web builds, just to test all that random yada.\r\n\r\n- Moves all the `AudioStream` related Resources to the `scene/resource/audio` folder and splits them into dedicated files\r\nSome like the WAV stream where already there, some where in the server folder.\r\n\r\n### Notes\r\n\r\nSpeaking of Resources, the audio server and system has a lot of legacy Resource mumbo. We shortly discussed in the audio dev channel why a server shouldn't depend directly on Resource at all so having them as part of the server folder is kinda misplaced.\r\n\r\nResource are user facing IO handles, they belong in the scene land, not the server land. A server should never have to use a Resources directly, it should always use either a `RID` handle or a `RefCounted` on its API. That the AudioServer has a lot of legacy where this is not followed is its own future issue to fix.\r\n\r\nThe `MovieWriter` includes suck but I found no less-than-dirty way around that since the virtual call breaks due to init problems as the enums are registered by the server and the moviewriter tries to be the cool guy that goes first for reasons.\r\n\r\nThat the AudioDriver and the Server used near duplicated enums ... that is something that should be tested and fixed. I just did not want to risk it here in the include chaos because I can't test all the builds local.\r\n\r\nNo AI was used, yada me surprised.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"220\" height=\"223\" alt=\"617275402-29f38e33-3ef5-480c-b904-1c1d7f334c98\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52bc954a-eaf6-4b8f-ac47-4442b379ab70\" />\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121547/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":7,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121547/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}